{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JDG",
  "chapter": 17,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JDG.17.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JDG.17.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And there was a man of mount Ephraim, whose name ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Micah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JDG.17.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JDG.17.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he said to his mother, The eleven hundred ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shekels",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of silver that were taken from thee, about which thou didst curse, and speak of also in my ears, behold, the silver ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with me; I took it. And his mother said, Blessed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be thou",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of the LORD, my son.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JDG.17.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JDG.17.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when he had restored the eleven hundred ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shekels",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of silver to his mother, his mother said, I had wholly dedicated the silver to the LORD from my hand for my son, to make a graven image and a molten image: now therefore I will restore it to thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JDG.17.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JDG.17.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yet he restored the money to his mother; and his mother took two hundred ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shekels",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of silver, and gave them to the founder, who made of it a graven image and a molten image: and they were in the house of Micah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JDG.17.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JDG.17.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the man Micah had a house of gods, and made an ephod, and teraphim, and consecrated one of his sons, who became his priest.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JDG.17.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JDG.17.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In those days ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no king in Israel, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "but",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " every man did ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that which was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " right in his own eyes.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JDG.17.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JDG.17.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And there was a young man out of Beth-lehem-judah of the family of Judah, who ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a Levite, and he sojourned there.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JDG.17.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JDG.17.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the man departed out of the city from Beth-lehem-judah, to sojourn where he could find ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "a place",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ": and he came to mount Ephraim to the house of Micah, as he journeyed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JDG.17.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JDG.17.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Micah said to him, Whence comest thou? And he said to him, I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a Levite of Beth-lehem-judah, and I go to sojourn where I may find ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "a place",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JDG.17.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JDG.17.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Micah said to him, Dwell with me, and be to me a father and a priest, and I will give thee ten ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shekels",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of silver by the year, and a suit of apparel, and thy victuals. So the Levite went in.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JDG.17.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JDG.17.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the Levite was content to dwell with the man; and the young man was to him as one of his sons.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JDG.17.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JDG.17.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Micah consecrated the Levite; and the young man became his priest, and was in the house of Micah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JDG.17.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JDG.17.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then said Micah, Now I know that the LORD will do me good, seeing I have a Levite for ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "my",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " priest.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
